.TH "PB-CONFIG-LOCAL-ACCESS" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-config-local-access - Configure the local browser domain


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb config local-access [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Configure the DNS domain this computer uses for private browser addresses such as https://3000.homelab.<domain>\&. Port names and a machine's front desk are stored on the server and set with \fBpb port name set\fR and \fBpb port front-desk\fR\&.

.PP
With --json, this command group lists its available commands.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for local-access


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print machine-readable JSON

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override

.PP
\fB--workspace\fP=""
	resource workspace selector: personal or a team slug


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb-config(1)\fP, \fBpb-config-local-access-domain(1)\fP, \fBpb-config-local-access-show(1)\fP
